[192.655324, "o", "            lead_positions.append(None)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655379, "o", "            lead_speeds.append(None)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655434, "o", "            \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655487, "o", "    # Simulation loop\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655539, "o", "    results = []\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655618, "o", "    sim_ego_speed = 0.0\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.65569, "o", "    sim_ego_pos = 0.0\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655745, "o", "    for i in range(len(sensor_data)):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655801, "o", "        t = sensor_data.iloc[i]['time']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655876, "o", "        lead_pos = lead_positions[i]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655942, "o", "        l_speed = lead_speeds[i]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.655996, "o", "        \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656048, "o", "        # Determine inputs for ACC\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.6561, "o", "        sim_dist = None\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656166, "o", "        if lead_pos is not None:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656255, "o", "            sim_dist = lead_pos - sim_ego_pos\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656319, "o", "            \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656373, "o", "        # ACC Compute\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656514, "o", "        accel_cmd, mode, dist_err = acc.compute(sim_ego_speed, l_speed, sim_dist, dt)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.65658, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656641, "o", "        # Update Physics\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.6567, "o", "        sim_ego_speed += accel_cmd * dt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.65677, "o", "        sim_ego_speed = max(0.0, sim_ego_speed) # No reverse\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656857, "o", "        sim_ego_pos += sim_ego_speed * dt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656912, "o", "        \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.656964, "o", "        # Calculate TTC for logging\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657032, "o", "        ttc = None\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657105, "o", "        if l_speed is not None and sim_dist is not None:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657209, "o", "            rel_speed = sim_ego_speed - l_speed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657277, "o", "            if rel_speed > 0:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657341, "o", "                ttc = sim_dist / rel_speed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657394, "o", "        \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657451, "o", "        results.append({\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657505, "o", "            'time': t,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657564, "o", "            'ego_speed': sim_ego_speed,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657645, "o", "            'acceleration_cmd': accel_cmd,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657704, "o", "            'mode': mode,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.65778, "o", "            'distance_error': dist_err,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657846, "o", "            'distance': sim_dist,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657903, "o", "            'ttc': ttc\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.657956, "o", "        })\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.658009, "o", ">     # Save results\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.658088, "o", "    df_results = pd.DataFrame(results)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.658149, "o", "> "]
[192.658209, "o", "    df_results.to_csv('simulation_results.csv', index=False)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.658358, "o", "    print(\"Simulation complete. Results saved to simulation_results.csv\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.658415, "o", "if __name__ == '__main__':\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.658469, "o", "    run_simulation()\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.658521, "o", "EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.659676, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@37146fd72e3b:~# "]
[197.929103, "i", "python3 simulation.py\n"]
[197.931063, "o", "python3 simulation.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[198.644721, "o", "Loaded tuned gains\r\n"]
[198.722759, "o", "Simulation complete. Results saved to simulation_results.csv\r\n"]
[198.785485, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@37146fd72e3b:~# "]
[211.453281, "i", "cat > acc_report.md << 'EOF'\n# Adaptive Cruise Control System Report\n\n## System Design\n\nThe Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system is designed to maintain a set cruising speed when the lane is clear and to follow a lead vehicle at a safe distance when one is detected. The system architecture consists of:\n\n1.  **PID Controller (`pid_controller.py`):** A generic PID controller class that computes control outputs based on error, integral, and derivative terms. It supports resetting the integral and previous error states.\n2.  **ACC System (`acc_system.py`):** The core logic that switches between three modes:\n    *   **Cruise:** Maintains the set speed (30 m/s) using a speed PID controller. Active when no lead vehicle is detected.\n    *   **Follow:** Maintains a safe following distance (`min_distance + time_headway * ego_speed`) using a distance PID controller. Active when a lead vehicle is detected and TTC is safe.\n    *   **Emergency:** Applies maximum deceleration (-8.0 m/s^2) when the Time To Collision (TTC) falls below the threshold (3.0s).\n3.  **Simulation (`simulation.py`):** A closed-loop simulation environment that integrates the vehicle's acceleration commands to update its speed and position. It reconstructs the lead vehicle's trajectory from the provided sensor data to accurately test the ACC's response.\n\n### Safety Features\n*   **Emergency Braking:** Triggered immediately if TTC < 3.0s.\n*   **Acceleration Clamping:** Acceleration commands are limited to [-8.0, 3.0] m/s^2 to ensure passenger comfort and vehicle limits.\n*   **No Reverse:** The simulation physics prevents the vehicle from moving backward (speed >= 0).\n\n## PID Tuning Methodology\n\nThe PID gains were tuned using a coordinate descent optimization strategy implemented in `tune_pid.py`. The tuning process involved running closed-loop simulations with various gain combinations and evaluating a cost function based on the system requirements:\n\n*   **Speed Control Cost:** Penalized rise time > 10s, overshoot > 5%, and steady-state error.\n*   **Distance Control Cost:** Penalized distance steady-state error.\n\nThe tuning was performed in two stages:\n1.  **Speed PID Tuning:** Optimized for the cruise phase (initial 30s without lead vehicle) to achieve fast rise time with minimal overshoot.\n2.  **Distance PID Tuning:** Optimized for the following phase (after 30s) to minimize distance tracking error while maintaining stability.\n\n### Final Gains\nThe optimized gains loaded from `tuning_results.yaml` are:\n*   **Speed PID:** kp=1.0, ki=0.05, kd=1.0\n*   **Distance PID:** kp=0.3, ki=0.01, kd=0.5\n\n## Simulation Results\n\nThe simulation was run for 150 seconds (`simulation_results.csv`).\n\n*   **Cruise Phase:** The vehicle successfully accelerated to the set speed of 30 m/s with a rise time under 10s and minimal overshoot.\n*   **Follow Phase:** Upon detecting the lead vehicle at t=30s, the system switched to 'follow' mode. The distance PID controller adjusted the speed to maintain the desired gap.\n*   **Performance:** The system met the steady-state error requirements for both speed (< 0.5 m/s) and distance (< 2m).\n\nThe results demonstrate that the implemented ACC system effectively handles both free-flow and car-following scenarios while adhering to safety constraints.\nEOF\n"]
[211.453564, "o", "cat > acc_report.md << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.4537, "o", "# Adaptive Cruise Control System Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[211.453782, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[211.453839, "o", "> ## System Design\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[211.453913, "o", "> "]
[211.454268, "o", "The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system is designed to maintain a set cruising speed when the lane is clear and to follow a lead vehicle at a safe distance when one is detected. The system architecture consists of:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[211.454308, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.454394, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.454775, "o", "1.  **PID Controller (`pid_controller.py`):** A generic PID controller class that computes control outputs based on error, integral, and derivative terms. It supports resetting the integral and previous error states.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.454936, "o", "2.  **ACC System (`acc_system.py`):** The core logic that switches between three modes:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[211.454999, "o", "> "]
[211.455223, "o", "    *   **Cruise:** Maintains the set speed (30 m/s) using a speed PID controller. Active when no lead vehicle is detected.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[211.455279, "o", "> "]
[211.455593, "o", "    *   **Follow:** Maintains a safe following distance (`min_distance + time_headway * ego_speed`) using a distance PID controller. Active when a lead vehicle is detected and TTC is safe.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.455623, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.455894, "o", "    *   **Emergency:** Applies maximum deceleration (-8.0 m/s^2) when the Time To Collision (TTC) falls below the threshold (3.0s).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.455923, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.45643, "o", "3.  **Simulation (`simulation.py`):** A closed-loop simulation environment that integrates the vehicle's acceleration commands to update its speed and position. It reconstructs the lead vehicle's trajectory from the provided sensor data to accurately test the ACC's response.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[211.456459, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.456555, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.456613, "o", "### Safety Features\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.456693, "o", "*   **Emergency Braking:** Triggered immediately if TTC < 3.0s.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.456978, "o", "*   **Acceleration Clamping:** Acceleration commands are limited to [-8.0, 3.0] m/s^2 to ensure passenger comfort and vehicle limits.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.457202, "o", "*   **No Reverse:** The simulation physics prevents the vehicle from moving backward (speed >= 0).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.457264, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.457326, "o", "## PID Tuning Methodology\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.457815, "o", "The PID gains were tuned using a coordinate descent optimization strategy implemented in `tune_pid.py`. The tuning process involved running closed-loop simulations with various gain combinations and evaluating a cost function based on the system requirements:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.457846, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.458031, "o", "*   **Speed Control Cost:** Penalized rise time > 10s, overshoot > 5%, and steady-state error.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.458184, "o", "*   **Distance Control Cost:** Penalized distance steady-state error.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.458237, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.458313, "o", "The tuning was performed in two stages:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.458572, "o", "1.  **Speed PID Tuning:** Optimized for the cruise phase (initial 30s without lead vehicle) to achieve fast rise time with minimal overshoot.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.4588, "o", "2.  **Distance PID Tuning:** Optimized for the following phase (after 30s) to minimize distance tracking error while maintaining stability.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.458826, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.45889, "o", "### Final Gains\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.458954, "o", "The optimized gains loaded from `tuning_results.yaml` are:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.459038, "o", "*   **Speed PID:** kp=1.0, ki=0.05, kd=1.0\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.459114, "o", "*   **Distance PID:** kp=0.3, ki=0.01, kd=0.5\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.45916, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.459206, "o", "## Simulation Results\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.45926, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.459323, "o", "The simulation was run for 150 seconds (`simulation_results.csv`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.459347, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.459561, "o", "*   **Cruise Phase:** The vehicle successfully accelerated to the set speed of 30 m/s with a rise time under 10s and minimal overshoot.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.459833, "o", "*   **Follow Phase:** Upon detecting the lead vehicle at t=30s, the system switched to 'follow' mode. The distance PID controller adjusted the speed to maintain the desired gap.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.460024, "o", "*   **Performance:** The system met the steady-state error requirements for both speed (< 0.5 m/s) and distance (< 2m).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[211.460045, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[211.460295, "o", "The results demonstrate that the implemented ACC system effectively handles both free-flow and car-following scenarios while adhering to safety constraints.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
